findings.body:
**Keep the persisted snapshot policy when a concurrent submission reuses the request ID.**

The `EEXIST` branch compares only `wire`. It does not compare `snapshotPolicy`, which is stored in the record but kept out of `wire`. Two invocations with the same `requestId` and identical wire selectors but different `reachable` values can therefore both pass. When the `reachable` invocation loses the race, it keeps its local `'reachable'` policy. It skips `captureSnapshot` and the scanner at line 193, then dispatches a request without a snapshot. The record written by the winning invocation still says `'snapshot'`. Sequential retries honor the saved policy, so the same `requestId` can yield different effective policies depending on timing.

Compare the stored policy in the `EEXIST` branch and reject a mismatch:

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
         } catch (error) {
           if ((error as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code !== 'EEXIST') throw error;
-          const concurrent = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, 'utf8')) as { wire: unknown };
-          if (!isDeepStrictEqual(concurrent.wire, wire))
+          const concurrent = JSON.parse(await readFile(path, 'utf8')) as {
+            wire: unknown;
+            snapshotPolicy?: string;
+          };
+          if (!isDeepStrictEqual(concurrent.wire, wire) || concurrent.snapshotPolicy !== snapshotPolicy)
             throw new Error('requestId is already bound to different inputs');
         }
```

</details>

Same-policy duplicate submissions still pass this check. The retry path at lines 106–128 is unchanged.
